{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795331631,"nonce":"xLxMI0iP8ZELPEOOp+P25kjyWi4=","title":"Webhook trigger runs before the delivery is answered: a dropped handler can lose the delivery","message":"From ADR-0081 revision (2026-11-22): ingest_event (crates/scarab-server/src/lib.rs ~8473) records the delivery id, then runs the trigger (which may call the forge compare API, up to 5 s) before answering the webhook. If the forge closes the connection and hyper drops the handler mid-trigger, the delivery id is recorded but no Run was created, and the redelivery is answered 'duplicate delivery'. Unverified whether hyper drops the handler on disconnect. Test: close the connection mid-compare and assert the Run still exists; if lost, move the trigger into a spawned task. Also check Forgejo's default DELIVER_TIMEOUT (believed 5 s, unverified) against the 5 s compare budget.","files":null}]}